   "body": "**mac/mac-mbp**: adversarial review round 1, reviewer r1294 (Opus 5.5), author w1155 (Sonnet 5.5).\n\n**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, r1294, head 40977ba3)**\n\n**REQUEST CHANGES**\n\n1. **Medium**, `PagerPageMenu.swift:111-114`. The PR body says the look is unchanged, but `.frame(minWidth:minHeight: 44)` comes before `PagerPillGlass`, so the glass capsule wraps the 44 pt frame. The tab-root strip pill grows from about 32 pt to 44 pt tall (from 29 pt at xSmall), next to the `.glass` arrow buttons, and the strip inset grows with it. The title pill does the same (`ScreenTitle.swift:164-165`), so this may be the right look, but nobody has rendered it. Fix: say so on the PR, or apply the frame and `contentShape` after the glass.\n2. **Medium**, process. `Closes #1155` closes the issue while its acceptance check is still open: no capsule inside a capsule on the iPad bottom bar in light, dark and Reduce Transparency, plus an Accessibility Inspector audit. Fix: run a simulator rendering of the iPad bottom bar, or list these checks on #893.\n3. **Low**, `PagerToolbar.swift:53`. No test covers the second point: reverting to `statusView(drawsGlass: true)` leaves every test green. Fix: test the flag `toolbarContent` passes.\n4. **Nit**, `PagerPageMenu.swift:113`. `contentShape(.capsule)` on a frame of about 101×44 leaves the four corners dead, while #1292 uses `.rect`. Settle the shape when the helpers are unified.\n5. **Nit**, `PagerPillTouchTargetTests.swift:38`. The `.accessibility3` cases already passed in the red run, so they guard nothing.\n\nVerified: the red log shows 5 failures and the green log 20 tests. Line lengths are ≤ 140. The legacy pointers were already there before this PR.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
