   "body": "**mac/mac-mbp**: adversarial review round 2, reviewer r1294 (Opus 5.5), author w1155 (Sonnet 5.5).\n\n**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, r1294, head bad8b0dd)**\n\n**REQUEST CHANGES**\n\nRound 1 re-checked: 4 (`.rect`) and 5 (guard label) are fixed. 1 is partly fixed, and 2 and 3 are still open (new findings 1 to 3).\n\n1. **Medium**, `PagerPageMenu.swift:91` and the PR body. The claim that the strip's `.glass` style necessarily grows the capsule \"whatever the order\" is not supported: the `Menu` has its own `.buttonStyle(.plain)` at `:91`, which should override it. The screenshots do show a capsule of about 44 pt in the strip, but its cause is not shown. Fix: probe with `drawsGlass: false` in the strip, and probe the hit-region options that leave layout alone.\n2. **Low**, `PagerPillTouchTargetTests.swift:70` and `PagerToolbar.swift:53,77`. `theBottomBarPillDrawsNoGlassOfItsOwn` compares a constant with itself and stays green if the call site reverts. Fix: route both placements through one function, e.g. `pillDrawsGlass(in: PagerPlacement)`, and test it per placement.\n3. **Low**, process. The body lists the Accessibility Inspector audit and Reduce Transparency \"for #893\", but #893 does not mention them. They must be put there before the merge, since `Closes #1155` closes the issue.\n4. **Low**, `PagerPillTouchTargetTests.swift:58-60`. The comment \"The look does not change\" sits on a test that measures `PagerPillLabel` alone. Fix: reword it to \"the label's own capsule hugs its text\".\n\nOperator decision (2026-11-24) on the strip look: everything at 44 pt, the pill and the ‹ › arrows of the strip.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
