   "body": "**mac/mac-mbp**: adversarial review round 3 (last), reviewer r1294 (Opus 5.5), author w1155 (Sonnet 5.5).\n\n**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, r1294, head 9be46f08)**\n\n**APPROVE**\n\nRound 2 re-checked:\n1. Fixed. The stated cause matches the code: `glassEffect` on the `Menu` label fills the Menu's 44 pt bounds, and the Menu's own `.plain` style (`PagerPageMenu.swift:91`) overrides the strip's `.glass`.\n2. Fixed. `pillDrawsGlass(in:)` (`PagerToolbar.swift:78`) is read only through `statusView(in:)`, for the bottom bar and for the strip. A call site passing the wrong placement would still not be caught.\n3. Fixed. #893 lists the device checks, and the operator decision is on #1155.\n4. Fixed. The test comment is reworded.\n\nNew (details):\n1. `PagerToolbar.swift:133`. The 20×30 inner minimum depends on the glass padding measured on iOS 27.2. The test pins the result at 44 to 45 pt, so an OS change will fail the test rather than go unnoticed. From the large size up, the symbol is bigger than the minimum and the arrows stay at least 44 pt.\n2. At 320 pt (Slide Over), the classic row with first and last needs about 335 pt, so `ViewThatFits` drops first and last. There is no overflow.\n\nVerified:\n- Arrow test red before the fix (34.7×28.7 at xSmall).\n- 25 tests green.\n- Cropped fix2 strip shots, light and dark: pill and arrows about 44 pt, one capsule each.\n- The wrapped call and the `stripArrow` signature compile by reading. No line over 140.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
